spinoza-god.md:3: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps spinoza-god.logic.r1.2 and spinoza-god.logic.r1.3, to: Suppose "God's essence involves existence", "necessarily, (if it is not so that God, or substance, consisting of infinite attributes, exists, then it is not so that God's essence involves existence)", "necessarily, (if it is not so that God, or substance, consisting of infinite attributes, exists, then it is not so that God's essence involves existence)" and "possibly, it is not so that God, or substance, consisting of infinite attributes, exists" are false. Is S4, "Proof.--If this be denied, conceive, if possible, that God does not exist: then his essence does not involve existence.", true then?
spinoza-god.md:3: argue/readings: S5 is read 2 ways: spinoza-god.logic.r1 has "essence_involves_existence"; spinoza-god.logic.r1.2 and spinoza-god.logic.r1.3 have "□essence_involves_existence"; they differ when only "God's essence involves existence" is true, which the first allows
spinoza-god.md:3: argue/modal-ambiguous: S5 is read spinoza-god.logic.r1 with no modality; spinoza-god.logic.r1.2 and spinoza-god.logic.r1.3 as what is necessary or possible: the text does not say which it means
